# A Stop hook that exits 2 continues the turn, as in Claude Code: its
# stderr goes back to the model as hidden feedback, the model answers again
# in the same turn, and the hook (now seeing stop_hook_active) lets it stop.
# The user sees a note with the hook's command and reason.
@faux testdata/faux/qa/stop-hook-continue.yaml
@setup printf 'if [ -e blocked-once ]; then exit 0; fi\ntouch blocked-once\necho add tests first >&2\nexit 2\n' > gate.sh
@setup mkdir -p .claude && printf '{"hooks":{"Stop":[{"hooks":[{"type":"command","command":"sh gate.sh"}]}]}}\n' > .claude/settings.json

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 20
SEND finish the feature
WAITFOR /Second pass, after the Stop hook asked for tests\./ 20
WAIT 1
SHOT continued
EXPECT /First pass done\./
EXPECT /Stop hook asked to continue: \[sh gate\.sh\]: add tests first/
EXPECT_NOT /esc to stop/
RUN test -e blocked-once
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
